Uf1cEi36p3HgmbQcHp","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_prepare_route","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":22,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've set up the route and it needs your approval before anything runs. Estimated total cost is **$10.22**, within your $15 policy limit.\n\nYour Robinhood (`rh1`) and Arbitrum (`arb1`) wallets have no ETH to pay transaction fees. So the route first sends 0.001 ETH to each one for fees. Smaller amounts were rejected because the bridge fee would have used up the whole transfer.\n\n| # | Step | In → out (estimated) | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `eth1`: swap ETH → WBTC | 0.1 ETH → 0.00495 WBTC | $3.90 |\n| 2 | Send ETH for fees, `eth1` → `rh1` | 0.001 ETH → 0.000833 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 3 | Send ETH for fees, `eth1` → `arb1` | 0.001 ETH → 0.000833 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 4 | Send WBTC, `eth1` → `rh1` | 0.002475 → 0.00246666 WBTC | $1.40 |\n| 5 | `rh1`: swap WBTC → ETH | → about 0.04923 ETH | $0.36 |\n| 6 | Send WBTC, `eth1` → `arb1` | 0.002475 → 0.00246666 WBTC | $1.40 |\n| 7 | `arb1`: swap WBTC → USDC | → about 147.70 USDC | $0.36 |\n\n**Expected end state:**\n- **`eth1`:** about 0.048 ETH, after fees.\n- **`rh1`:** about 0.0501 ETH.\n- **`arb1`:** about 147.70 USDC, plus about 0.0008 ETH for future fees.\n\nThe cheaper-looking option for the USDC half cost more. Swapping to USDC on Ethereum and then bridging it adds about $3.54, and Arbitrum would still need ETH for fees.\n\nReply **approve**, **reject**, or give a cost cap. These prices expire in 5 minutes, so if you approve after that I'll get new ones first."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":23,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":24,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_10"},"id":"toolu_01B98hB3U4eiCfRrnX3iKe7D"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":25,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"tx_id\":\"tx_11\"}","toolCallId":